// Poolit: every gate a request passes, and what each one refuses
// Diagram type: Flow chart (Eraser diagram-as-code)
// Each gate below is covered by an automated test; breaking a gate on purpose makes the test fail.

title Poolit security layers
direction down
colorMode bold
styleMode shadow
typeface clean

Request [shape: oval, icon: arrow-right, color: blue, label: "Request from a browser or phone"]

Role [shape: diamond, icon: key, color: blue, label: "Signed in? (login token)"]
Visitor [icon: user, color: gray, label: "Runs as anon (visitor)"]
Signed in [icon: user-check, color: green, label: "Runs as authenticated, caller id from the token"]

Permission [shape: diamond, icon: lock, color: blue, label: "May this role run this function?"]
Refuse 401 [shape: oval, icon: x-circle, color: red, label: "401 refused: only 8 functions are open to visitors"]

Identity [shape: diamond, icon: shield, color: blue, label: "Vendor function: is the caller linked to this store, with the right role?"]
Refuse 403 [shape: oval, icon: x-circle, color: red, label: "403 refused: other store, student, or staff doing owner work"]

Validate [shape: diamond, icon: check-square, color: blue, label: "Valid input? (types, ranges, lengths, whole numbers)"]
Refuse 400 [shape: oval, icon: x-circle, color: red, label: "400 refused: bad input, nothing changed"]

Rules [shape: diamond, icon: sliders, color: blue, label: "Business rules (stock, pool open, 3 orders per student per pool, delivery state)"]
Refuse 409 [shape: oval, icon: x-circle, color: red, label: "409 refused: whole change rolled back"]

Server function [icon: key, color: green, label: "Server only function runs, row locked, all or nothing"]
Tables [icon: database, color: green, label: "Closed tables: row security on, no grants, no policies"]
Answer [shape: oval, icon: check-circle, color: green, label: "Answer shaped by private helpers: no emails or phone numbers of other people"]

// ---------------- Storage gate ----------------

Upload [shape: oval, icon: upload, color: blue, label: "Vendor uploads a picture"]
Upload rule [shape: diamond, icon: image, color: blue, label: "Own store folder? Name matches the pattern? JPEG or WebP? 200 KB or less?"]
Upload refused [shape: oval, icon: x-circle, color: red, label: "Refused: no overwrite and no delete through the API either"]
Stored [shape: oval, icon: check-circle, color: green, label: "Stored, public to read, cached for a year"]

// ---------------- Never exposed ----------------

Never exposed [icon: eye-off, color: gray, label: "Never reachable from a browser: private schema, server only functions, service role key, backups"]

// ---------------- Flow ----------------

Request > Role
Role > Visitor: no
Role > Signed in: yes
Visitor > Permission
Signed in > Permission
Permission > Refuse 401: no
Permission > Identity: yes
Identity > Refuse 403: no
Identity > Validate: yes
Validate > Refuse 400: no
Validate > Rules: yes
Rules > Refuse 409: no
Rules > Server function: yes
Server function > Tables
Tables > Answer

Upload > Upload rule
Upload rule > Upload refused: no
Upload rule > Stored: yes

Server function > Never exposed: stays inside the database
